            "notable": "The Oracle MDM cost twice: an expensive licence, and a team employed full-time to correct the data it produced. [[Replacing it meant rebuilding a mature product's behaviour with no specification to work from — documentation was absent or years stale, so the incumbent's real rules had to be recovered from the system itself.]]\n\nThe house standard was Spring on a dedicated external Tomcat, on ageing on-premise infrastructure. I argued for Spring Boot with embedded Tomcat instead — the better fit, and the furthest the client would go. With a mostly junior team on a critical system, a from-scratch rebuild on a current stack was also the one chance they'd get to learn one.",
